.el .ds Aq '
.TH nut-events 1  "nut-cli 0.1.0" nut
.SH NAME
nut\-events \- Show UPS event history
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnut events\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-boot\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-follow\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-outages\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-raw\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-last\-outage\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show UPS event history
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Color output policy
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-since\fR \fI<TIME>\fR
Include entries since a journalctl time (for example, \*(Aqtoday\*(Aq or \*(Aq\-2h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use ASCII symbols and bars
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-boot\fR \fI<N>\fR
Select a boot offset (0 is current, \-1 is previous)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-follow\fR
Stream new entries and updated stories until interrupted
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON where supported
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-outages\fR
Show only power outages, blips, and shutdowns
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Include additional diagnostic detail
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read host settings from this file
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-raw\fR
Show source journal messages instead of stories
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR
Maximum stories or raw entries to show (1\-2000; default 20)
.TP
\fB\-\-last\-outage\fR
Show only the most recent outage (alias for \-\-outages \-\-limit 1)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRA
System journal access may require sudo nut events. Optional systemd\-journal membership exposes all system logs; nut never changes it automatically.
